1
00:00:04,867 --> 00:00:11,800
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:31,800 --> 00:00:32,767
[TIRES SCREECHING]

3
00:00:34,100 --> 00:00:35,067
[ENGINE REVVING]

4
00:00:39,833 --> 00:00:40,933
[TIRES SCREECH]

5
00:00:42,333 --> 00:00:44,100
[ENGINES REVVING]

6
00:00:44,100 --> 00:00:45,300
[TRUCK HORN BLARES]

7
00:00:45,300 --> 00:00:46,433
[LOUD CRASH]

8
00:00:46,800 --> 00:00:48,133
[TIRES SCREECHING]

9
00:00:50,633 --> 00:00:51,633
[GUNSHOT]

10
00:00:52,567 --> 00:00:53,633
[FIREWORKS EXPLODING]

11
00:00:53,633 --> 00:00:55,333
- [ENGINES REVVING]
- [BUS HORN HONKS]

12
00:00:56,600 --> 00:00:58,000
[GLASS SHATTERING]

13
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:00,133
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [LOUD CRASH]

14
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:02,700
[ENGINES REVVING]

15
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:06,167
[TIRES SCREECHING]

16
00:01:07,167 --> 00:01:09,067
[TIRES SCREECHING]

17
00:01:10,033 --> 00:01:11,567
- [GUNSHOT]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

18
00:01:11,567 --> 00:01:13,133
- [TRUCK HORN BLARES]
- [LOUD CRASH]

19
00:01:13,133 --> 00:01:14,600
[TIRES SCREECHING]

20
00:01:20,233 --> 00:01:22,167
<i>We actually wanted
to talk to your husband</i>

21
00:01:22,167 --> 00:01:23,200
<i> about what happened.</i>

22
00:01:23,200 --> 00:01:24,233
<i> To settle things?</i>

23
00:01:24,233 --> 00:01:26,233
<i> It'll be easier to talk
to Rudy if...</i>

24
00:01:26,233 --> 00:01:27,333
<i> Here you go.</i>

25
00:01:27,333 --> 00:01:30,033
<i> You'll get their sweet yeses.</i>

26
00:01:30,033 --> 00:01:31,700
<i> Too bad. Nice try, though.</i>

27
00:01:31,700 --> 00:01:34,000
<i>- One more game?
- Let's play again, Mister Rudy!</i>

28
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:35,400
<i> Can you tell us what happened?</i>

29
00:01:35,400 --> 00:01:38,233
<i> A man helped us.</i>

30
00:01:38,233 --> 00:01:40,433
<i>He even promised to help
with the cost of the surgery.</i>

31
00:01:40,467 --> 00:01:43,033
<i>The records clearly state that
you made an unauthorized arrest.</i>

32
00:01:43,033 --> 00:01:45,467
<i>All I wanted was
to catch Mr. Chan.</i>

33
00:01:45,467 --> 00:01:48,533
<i> Mr. Chan's testimony
will determine your fate.</i>

34
00:01:48,533 --> 00:01:49,567
<i> Kill them.</i>

35
00:01:49,567 --> 00:01:50,567
<i>- No! No!
- No, please!</i>

36
00:01:50,567 --> 00:01:51,567
<i> Here's what we're going to do.</i>

37
00:01:51,567 --> 00:01:52,733
<i> We'll try to befriend Gabo.</i>

38
00:01:52,733 --> 00:01:53,867
<i> If you let us go...</i>

39
00:01:53,867 --> 00:01:56,233
<i> We can spy on Gabo for you.</i>

40
00:01:56,233 --> 00:01:58,467
<i>I realized that life here
outside is much harder.</i>

41
00:01:58,467 --> 00:01:59,900
<i> I can give you a mission.</i>

42
00:01:59,900 --> 00:02:01,667
<i>But I don't know
if you're ready.</i>

43
00:02:01,667 --> 00:02:03,133
<i>Gabo won't be able
to handle this mission.</i>

44
00:02:03,133 --> 00:02:04,900
<i> Pops, the decision is yours.</i>

45
00:02:07,400 --> 00:02:09,267
- [INDISTINCT CROWD CHATTER]
- [PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

46
00:02:09,267 --> 00:02:11,033
- We stink!
- That was disgusting!

47
00:02:11,033 --> 00:02:12,033
- [GROANS]
- [SPITS]

48
00:02:12,033 --> 00:02:13,600
- Move it!
- We smell like fish!

49
00:02:14,867 --> 00:02:15,967
Hey, wait a minute.

50
00:02:15,967 --> 00:02:17,833
I'm confused by what
you said to Django.

51
00:02:18,200 --> 00:02:20,833
Be honest. Are we really
going to spy on Gabo?

52
00:02:20,833 --> 00:02:22,367
We're already working
for him, remember?

53
00:02:22,367 --> 00:02:24,133
But now you want us
to spy on him?

54
00:02:24,133 --> 00:02:26,400
What, are we double agents now?

55
00:02:26,400 --> 00:02:27,533
It's so confusing!

56
00:02:27,533 --> 00:02:29,067
Wasn't I obvious enough?

57
00:02:29,067 --> 00:02:32,333
I only said that so Django
wouldn't finish us off!

58
00:02:32,333 --> 00:02:34,233
So we're not actually
going to spy on Gabo?

59
00:02:34,233 --> 00:02:35,333
No!

60
00:02:35,333 --> 00:02:36,933
I just told him that

61
00:02:36,933 --> 00:02:39,033
so Django would think
we're on his side,

62
00:02:39,033 --> 00:02:40,167
when in fact...

63
00:02:40,700 --> 00:02:41,833
we're on Team Gabo.

64
00:02:41,833 --> 00:02:42,967
- Team Gabo?
- We're on his side!

65
00:02:42,967 --> 00:02:44,067
Sounds like we're in a fan club.

66
00:02:44,067 --> 00:02:45,167
We're called the Gabonatics.

67
00:02:45,167 --> 00:02:46,433
Sure, whatever that is.

68
00:02:46,433 --> 00:02:48,600
- I was very confused, man.
- Save your questions for later.

69
00:02:48,633 --> 00:02:49,767
They might come back after us.

70
00:02:49,767 --> 00:02:51,633
- Team Gabo Worldwide!
- Let's go!

71
00:02:51,867 --> 00:02:53,667
And you believed them?

72
00:02:53,667 --> 00:02:55,467
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

73
00:02:55,467 --> 00:02:56,600
No, Pa.

74
00:02:56,900 --> 00:02:58,400
I was just going along
with them.

75
00:02:58,767 --> 00:03:01,600
It's only right that
you don't trust them.

76
00:03:02,200 --> 00:03:05,200
They already broke away from us

77
00:03:05,200 --> 00:03:06,967
and then joined Gabo.

78
00:03:06,967 --> 00:03:08,100
So now...

79
00:03:09,033 --> 00:03:13,067
we don't even know
where their loyalty lies.

80
00:03:13,067 --> 00:03:14,367
[DJANGO] I know that.

81
00:03:15,333 --> 00:03:17,200
I only made them think

82
00:03:17,200 --> 00:03:19,900
that I believed every word
they said.

83
00:03:19,900 --> 00:03:21,233
But the truth is...

84
00:03:21,267 --> 00:03:22,900
- [CHUCKLES]
- [BOTTLE CLINKS]

85
00:03:22,900 --> 00:03:24,133
[OMINOUS MUSIC CONTINUES]

86
00:03:24,133 --> 00:03:26,033
I was just lowering
their defenses.

87
00:03:26,033 --> 00:03:28,500
[IBYANG] I don't support
the decisions you both make.

88
00:03:28,500 --> 00:03:30,200
Let's start with your father.

89
00:03:30,200 --> 00:03:32,233
He's trying to befriend Betchay.

90
00:03:32,233 --> 00:03:33,833
And here you are,

91
00:03:33,833 --> 00:03:37,300
reaching out
to Gabo's new friends.

92
00:03:37,700 --> 00:03:38,667
[DJANGO CHUCKLES]

93
00:03:38,667 --> 00:03:41,700
Look, we managed
to fool Gabo once.

94
00:03:42,233 --> 00:03:44,467
I'm just following
Papa's advice.

95
00:03:44,467 --> 00:03:46,500
It's not always
about throwing hands.

96
00:03:46,500 --> 00:03:48,300
You've got to use
your brain too.

97
00:03:50,133 --> 00:03:51,567
- [PAQUITO EXHALES]
- [GENTLE THUD]

98
00:03:51,567 --> 00:03:54,533
[MUSIC SWELLING]

99
00:03:54,567 --> 00:03:55,567
[MUSIC FADES]

100
00:03:56,667 --> 00:03:57,733
Phew!

101
00:03:57,733 --> 00:03:58,933
Hey, Rudy.

102
00:03:58,933 --> 00:04:02,033
You've been gone for a while.
I've been waiting.

103
00:04:02,033 --> 00:04:03,467
So where's the medicine
you bought?

104
00:04:03,467 --> 00:04:04,800
[DANTE] You should've told me.

105
00:04:04,800 --> 00:04:06,833
I could've bought it instead.

106
00:04:06,833 --> 00:04:08,400
It would've been way quicker.

107
00:04:08,400 --> 00:04:10,633
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

108
00:04:10,633 --> 00:04:12,667
Why? What happened?

109
00:04:13,233 --> 00:04:15,800
I passed by a group
of men playing cards.

110
00:04:16,100 --> 00:04:17,133
What?

111
00:04:17,467 --> 00:04:19,433
I got to tempted
to play because...

112
00:04:19,433 --> 00:04:21,100
I wanted to triple the money

113
00:04:21,100 --> 00:04:23,167
so that Betchay wouldn't have
anything to say.

114
00:04:23,167 --> 00:04:25,533
The problem is... I lost.

115
00:04:25,533 --> 00:04:26,533
Rudy...

116
00:04:27,233 --> 00:04:29,500
When did you get back
to gambling?

117
00:04:29,900 --> 00:04:31,000
[ELTON] Listen, Rudy.

118
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:34,700
You can't keep counting on luck,

119
00:04:34,700 --> 00:04:36,100
especially when it comes
to gambling.

120
00:04:36,100 --> 00:04:37,867
Winning there is
nearly impossible.

121
00:04:37,867 --> 00:04:40,400
That money was supposed
to be for medicine.

122
00:04:40,900 --> 00:04:44,433
[DANTE] You know, Rudy,
Gabo worked hard to earn it.

123
00:04:44,433 --> 00:04:45,633
What a waste...

124
00:04:45,633 --> 00:04:47,467
What would Gabo say about this?

125
00:04:47,467 --> 00:04:54,100
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

126
00:04:54,100 --> 00:04:55,767
- [DOOR CREAKS OPEN]
- [OLI SIGHS]

127
00:04:56,233 --> 00:04:57,833
Okay.

128
00:04:58,700 --> 00:04:59,800
- Okay. [CHUCKLES]
- [DOOR CREAKING]

129
00:04:59,800 --> 00:05:00,800
- Bro.
- [DOOR CLOSES]

130
00:05:00,800 --> 00:05:02,500
We got a good scoop.

131
00:05:03,300 --> 00:05:08,633
Stories like that are close
to the hearts of the masses.

132
00:05:08,633 --> 00:05:09,600
[CLEARS THROAT]

133
00:05:09,600 --> 00:05:10,667
Bro...

134
00:05:10,667 --> 00:05:12,167
It looks like...
[CLEARS THROAT]

135
00:05:12,167 --> 00:05:13,833
You're deep in thought.

136
00:05:14,500 --> 00:05:16,267
Are you still worried
about the gunshot victim?

137
00:05:16,267 --> 00:05:18,133
Actually, that's not what
I'm thinking about.

138
00:05:18,433 --> 00:05:19,500
It's Gabo.

139
00:05:20,400 --> 00:05:22,167
The one who helped the victim.

140
00:05:22,167 --> 00:05:24,800
Hmm? Maybe you just
find him handsome.

141
00:05:25,267 --> 00:05:26,967
Come to think of it,
he is good-looking.

142
00:05:26,967 --> 00:05:28,967
What I'm really thinking is...

143
00:05:29,467 --> 00:05:32,067
He also helped me
when I was ambushed.

144
00:05:32,067 --> 00:05:34,300
Doesn't that make him
a brave and good man?

145
00:05:34,333 --> 00:05:36,100
Gabo is impressive.

146
00:05:36,800 --> 00:05:40,333
He's got the looks
and the courage.

147
00:05:40,933 --> 00:05:42,300
- Lucky him!
- Lucky him!

148
00:05:42,667 --> 00:05:44,800
I know what to do.

149
00:05:44,800 --> 00:05:46,567
- Hmm?
- Call the writer.

150
00:05:46,567 --> 00:05:48,100
Let's have him featured
in the next episode.

151
00:05:48,100 --> 00:05:49,633
- I like that.
- Go.

152
00:05:49,633 --> 00:05:51,067
Alright, alright, alright.

153
00:05:52,133 --> 00:05:53,867
How old are you, Gabo?

154
00:05:54,433 --> 00:05:55,633
Twenty-eight.

155
00:05:55,633 --> 00:05:57,833
You remind me of my son.

156
00:05:58,667 --> 00:06:00,067
[PAPANG] His name is Danilo.

157
00:06:00,067 --> 00:06:01,067
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC PLAYING]

158
00:06:01,067 --> 00:06:03,233
<i> More than anything else,</i>

159
00:06:05,733 --> 00:06:09,400
he was the most important
person in my life.

160
00:06:09,967 --> 00:06:11,200
We're the same.

161
00:06:12,033 --> 00:06:14,033
My family is the most
important thing to me.

162
00:06:14,700 --> 00:06:15,833
But now,

163
00:06:15,833 --> 00:06:17,867
it's just my father
who's still with me.

164
00:06:17,867 --> 00:06:20,400
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

165
00:06:20,400 --> 00:06:22,000
Where's your mother?

166
00:06:22,000 --> 00:06:24,467
[MUSIC FADING]

167
00:06:24,467 --> 00:06:30,900
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

168
00:06:30,900 --> 00:06:32,133
She's gone.

169
00:06:34,167 --> 00:06:36,500
The police killed her.

170
00:06:39,000 --> 00:06:42,300
Up to now, I still haven't given
justice to her death.

171
00:06:45,633 --> 00:06:48,100
Fate can be cruel.

172
00:06:48,100 --> 00:06:50,500
We share the same tragedy.

173
00:06:50,500 --> 00:06:51,533
[GABO] Why?

174
00:06:51,533 --> 00:06:53,300
What happened to your family?

175
00:06:53,767 --> 00:06:54,967
[OMENG] Gabo.

176
00:06:54,967 --> 00:06:59,467
His wife and son were killed
without mercy.

177
00:07:00,233 --> 00:07:04,633
[PAPANG]<i> At the time, I believed
</i> we were destined to succeed.

178
00:07:04,633 --> 00:07:09,133
<i> My son had the resolve to face
the challenge I gave him.</i>

179
00:07:09,133 --> 00:07:13,167
<i> But before he could fulfill
his mission,</i>

180
00:07:13,167 --> 00:07:14,867
<i> they ambushed us.</i>

181
00:07:14,900 --> 00:07:18,167
<i> They took my son's life.</i>

182
00:07:18,167 --> 00:07:20,167
<i> They also took my wife's.</i>

183
00:07:20,800 --> 00:07:23,800
<i> They thought they had
killed me, too.</i>

184
00:07:26,300 --> 00:07:27,733
[OMENG] To this day,

185
00:07:27,733 --> 00:07:29,833
he is still seeking justice.

186
00:07:29,833 --> 00:07:31,800
I lost so much, Gabo.

187
00:07:31,800 --> 00:07:32,967
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

188
00:07:32,967 --> 00:07:34,800
I lost...

189
00:07:35,967 --> 00:07:37,200
my loved ones.

190
00:07:40,100 --> 00:07:43,100
That's why...

191
00:07:45,633 --> 00:07:47,733
I no longer want to live.

192
00:07:48,867 --> 00:07:50,633
But I have no choice now.

193
00:07:50,933 --> 00:07:52,700
If I give in,

194
00:07:53,100 --> 00:07:57,333
nothing will ever change
in our country.

195
00:07:57,333 --> 00:07:59,800
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

196
00:07:59,800 --> 00:08:03,300
That's why we need
your help, Gabo.

197
00:08:03,933 --> 00:08:09,667
We must bring justice to all
who are oppressed,

198
00:08:09,933 --> 00:08:11,967
all who are abused,

199
00:08:11,967 --> 00:08:16,467
and all who need our help.

200
00:08:17,833 --> 00:08:20,300
As long as our nation
remains in poverty,

201
00:08:22,233 --> 00:08:24,433
I see no hope.

202
00:08:25,500 --> 00:08:27,667
We need to take action, Gabo.

203
00:08:28,000 --> 00:08:33,633
The Filipino people need you.

204
00:08:33,633 --> 00:08:40,633
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

205
00:08:44,167 --> 00:08:48,567
During these times,
it's surprising to think...

206
00:08:48,567 --> 00:08:52,567
...that there are still people
who are willing to help

207
00:08:52,567 --> 00:08:54,367
without asking for anything
in exchange.

208
00:08:54,400 --> 00:08:55,900
They're a good samaritan.

209
00:08:56,633 --> 00:08:59,233
I met this man
when I responded

210
00:08:59,233 --> 00:09:02,233
to a stickup situation
in Ginintuang Lupa.

211
00:09:02,233 --> 00:09:04,267
His name is Gabo.

212
00:09:04,900 --> 00:09:08,900
- If I only had a picture--
- [ARNEL] Cut! Cut! Cut!

213
00:09:08,900 --> 00:09:10,400
I didn't approve of this.

214
00:09:10,400 --> 00:09:12,800
Why are you going
with this angle?

215
00:09:12,800 --> 00:09:14,833
Boss, this is the new angle.

216
00:09:14,833 --> 00:09:17,100
If you want to market someone...

217
00:09:17,633 --> 00:09:20,100
...market yourself, not others!

218
00:09:20,100 --> 00:09:23,200
But this is my show!
I know what I should report!

219
00:09:23,200 --> 00:09:25,733
Oh, so you're acting
arrogant now?

220
00:09:25,733 --> 00:09:27,000
Salvador!

221
00:09:27,000 --> 00:09:29,700
Remember, you may be the face,

222
00:09:29,733 --> 00:09:32,167
but I'm still the brains
of this show!

223
00:09:32,167 --> 00:09:36,533
You don't give the audience
an ally.

224
00:09:36,533 --> 00:09:38,233
You give them enemies!

225
00:09:38,767 --> 00:09:41,233
Writer! Writer!

226
00:09:45,900 --> 00:09:47,967
- Mr. Chan!
- Why so low?

227
00:09:47,967 --> 00:09:49,467
[LOCK RATTLING]

228
00:09:49,467 --> 00:09:50,767
[GATE CREAKS OPEN]

229
00:09:52,967 --> 00:09:54,233
Victor!

230
00:09:54,800 --> 00:09:55,900
[HANDCUFFS RATTLING]

231
00:09:55,900 --> 00:09:58,667
You are going down!

232
00:09:58,667 --> 00:09:59,967
Down!

233
00:10:01,200 --> 00:10:02,300
Mr. Chan!

234
00:10:03,300 --> 00:10:04,600
We're not done yet.

235
00:10:05,400 --> 00:10:06,600
No!

236
00:10:06,600 --> 00:10:10,400
You are done! I'm out! Bye!

237
00:10:14,500 --> 00:10:18,700
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

238
00:10:18,700 --> 00:10:20,500
[PIA] I'll get
the report ready, sir.

239
00:10:20,500 --> 00:10:21,767
[DELGADO] Okay. Thank you.

240
00:10:28,800 --> 00:10:30,000
Listen up.

241
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:32,300
Our target is Mr. Chan.

242
00:10:32,300 --> 00:10:34,767
Eliminate anyone
who will try to stop you.

243
00:10:35,533 --> 00:10:36,567
[GOONS] Yes, boss!

244
00:10:37,133 --> 00:10:41,633
Mr. Chan should not arrive
at his destination.

245
00:10:41,633 --> 00:10:43,533
Alright, men! Let's go!

246
00:10:47,800 --> 00:10:50,100
[DELGADO] Okay, men,
you have your orders.

247
00:10:50,100 --> 00:10:55,667
Make sure you'll bring Mr. Chan
to the safe house safely.

248
00:10:55,667 --> 00:10:58,467
Surveillance will be 24/7.

249
00:10:58,467 --> 00:11:03,767
No one can approach him.
Do you understand?

250
00:11:03,767 --> 00:11:04,933
Yes, sir!

251
00:11:06,467 --> 00:11:08,067
[TIRES SCREECHING]

252
00:11:08,100 --> 00:11:10,500
[ENGINES REVVING]

253
00:11:10,500 --> 00:11:13,267
- What about backup?
- That's just one person.

254
00:11:14,033 --> 00:11:16,233
Mariano can handle that.

255
00:11:16,233 --> 00:11:20,333
[OMINOUS MUSIC CONTINUES]

256
00:11:20,333 --> 00:11:21,800
We'll take care of you.

257
00:11:24,300 --> 00:11:25,500
Alright, you may go.

258
00:11:28,033 --> 00:11:34,967
[OMINOUS MUSIC CONTINUES]

259
00:11:37,433 --> 00:11:40,100
[OMENG] Gabo?
The people in position today...

260
00:11:40,600 --> 00:11:45,167
They take advantage
of people's weaknesses.

261
00:11:45,200 --> 00:11:47,933
That is the reality
of the Philippines today.

262
00:11:48,900 --> 00:11:51,867
They're backed
by powerful people

263
00:11:51,867 --> 00:11:54,000
whom you have to fight against.

264
00:11:54,000 --> 00:11:57,200
People who are powerful
and wealthy.

265
00:11:57,200 --> 00:11:59,100
Cold-blooded people

266
00:11:59,100 --> 00:12:03,467
whose souls are scattered
across the streets.

267
00:12:04,900 --> 00:12:07,333
[ARTURO] Sir, Mr. Chan
has left the NCIA.

268
00:12:08,100 --> 00:12:09,667
Are they still going
on the same route?

269
00:12:09,667 --> 00:12:10,833
Yes, sir. It's the same route.

270
00:12:11,700 --> 00:12:13,867
Hurry up. We have to catch them!

271
00:12:13,867 --> 00:12:14,933
[DRIVER] Yes, boss.

272
00:12:16,133 --> 00:12:19,400
[ENGINE REVVING]

273
00:12:19,400 --> 00:12:26,367
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

274
00:12:35,133 --> 00:12:37,200
[CAR WINDOW SLIDES DOWN]

275
00:12:39,400 --> 00:12:41,633
[OMENG] Gabo, don't worry.

276
00:12:41,633 --> 00:12:43,100
We are right behind you.

277
00:12:43,733 --> 00:12:44,967
But, you know...

278
00:12:45,467 --> 00:12:48,433
You are very different from
those who've tried this mission.

279
00:12:48,467 --> 00:12:54,200
However, you need to
study everything carefully.

280
00:12:54,200 --> 00:12:56,100
[UWAK] Remember this, Gabo.

281
00:12:56,100 --> 00:12:58,867
No one should know
your mission.

282
00:12:58,867 --> 00:13:02,367
When you enter this job,
you're on your own.

283
00:13:02,967 --> 00:13:04,300
You can't back out.

284
00:13:04,300 --> 00:13:06,867
You're responsible
for your own actions.

285
00:13:08,600 --> 00:13:11,300
[OMENG] Compared to what
we paid

286
00:13:11,300 --> 00:13:12,433
for your previous mission,

287
00:13:13,100 --> 00:13:14,233
your pay's bigger now.

288
00:13:15,200 --> 00:13:18,100
One million pesos

289
00:13:18,100 --> 00:13:20,333
for every mission
you accomplish.

290
00:13:22,133 --> 00:13:23,733
Think about it carefully.

291
00:13:23,733 --> 00:13:27,333
Someone who knows
how to take a stand

292
00:13:27,333 --> 00:13:29,267
is what our country needs now.

293
00:13:32,900 --> 00:13:34,200
[GABO] I need a job.

294
00:13:35,233 --> 00:13:36,567
That's why I came here.

295
00:13:37,900 --> 00:13:39,767
But I'm shocked at your offer.

296
00:13:40,400 --> 00:13:43,133
It's a big pay
for just one mission.

297
00:13:43,767 --> 00:13:45,200
It just means that...

298
00:13:45,767 --> 00:13:47,700
my life will be the price
for this.

299
00:13:50,167 --> 00:13:51,533
But don't worry, Pops.

300
00:13:53,133 --> 00:13:55,167
I accept your challenge.

301
00:13:57,700 --> 00:14:00,833
I won't do this just for myself
and my family.

302
00:14:01,400 --> 00:14:02,633
I will do this...

303
00:14:04,267 --> 00:14:05,933
...for all Filipinos.

304
00:14:07,867 --> 00:14:10,867
We need to put an end
to all the bad guys out there.

305
00:14:10,867 --> 00:14:12,933
We need to cleanse
our society

306
00:14:13,767 --> 00:14:15,533
and fix the entire Philippines.

307
00:14:16,767 --> 00:14:17,833
[OMENG CLEARS THROAT]

308
00:14:21,867 --> 00:14:23,200
[ENVELOPE SLIDES]

309
00:14:23,200 --> 00:14:25,567
[PAPANG] Sign the contract.

310
00:14:26,467 --> 00:14:33,367
[THRILLING MUSIC PLAYING]

311
00:14:36,633 --> 00:14:37,667
Pen.

312
00:14:39,700 --> 00:14:40,900
No need for that.

313
00:14:40,900 --> 00:14:42,867
[KNIFE RATTLING]

314
00:14:44,633 --> 00:14:50,167
[THRILLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

315
00:14:50,167 --> 00:14:51,200
[FLESH SLICES]

316
00:15:01,100 --> 00:15:06,667
[BLOOD DRIPPING SLOWLY]

317
00:15:06,667 --> 00:15:07,867
[GABO] This blood...

318
00:15:09,367 --> 00:15:11,567
<i>...is my symbol
of loyalty to you.</i>

319
00:15:15,267 --> 00:15:16,633
I promise.

320
00:15:19,100 --> 00:15:20,433
I won't let you down.

321
00:15:22,367 --> 00:15:27,267
[THRILLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

322
00:15:31,900 --> 00:15:38,200
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

323
00:15:42,067 --> 00:15:44,133
Sir, Mr. Chan's convoy
is approaching.

324
00:15:44,133 --> 00:15:49,833
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

325
00:15:49,833 --> 00:15:51,933
Bring me Mr. Chan.

326
00:15:51,933 --> 00:15:53,100
Yes, sir.

327
00:15:57,633 --> 00:15:59,033
[TIRES SCREECH]

328
00:16:00,667 --> 00:16:04,233
[GUNSHOTS]

329
00:16:04,767 --> 00:16:06,167
- I don't want to die!
- [GUNSHOTS]

330
00:16:06,167 --> 00:16:08,133
- I don't want to die!
- [TIRES SCREECH]

331
00:16:08,167 --> 00:16:09,767
[GUNSHOTS]

332
00:16:09,767 --> 00:16:11,733
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [GUNSHOTS]

333
00:16:12,900 --> 00:16:14,200
[BRAKES SCREECH]

334
00:16:14,200 --> 00:16:15,633
[GUNSHOTS]

335
00:16:20,667 --> 00:16:24,467
[GUNSHOTS]

336
00:16:24,467 --> 00:16:25,433
[BODY THUDS]

337
00:16:26,267 --> 00:16:32,000
[GUNSHOTS]

338
00:16:32,833 --> 00:16:34,100
[MR. CHAN WHIMPERS]

339
00:16:34,100 --> 00:16:39,900
[GUNSHOTS]

340
00:16:39,900 --> 00:16:40,900
[BODY THUDS]

341
00:16:40,900 --> 00:16:44,000
[GUNSHOTS]

342
00:16:44,033 --> 00:16:45,233
[MR. CHAN] Don't hurt me!

343
00:16:45,233 --> 00:16:46,833
- Don't hurt me!
- Mr. Chan!

344
00:16:48,133 --> 00:16:49,567
Don't kill me!
Don't kill me!

345
00:16:49,567 --> 00:16:51,333
Don't kill me!
I'll give you money!

346
00:16:51,333 --> 00:16:52,267
I'll give you money!

347
00:16:52,267 --> 00:16:54,067
I'll give you money!
Don't kill me!

348
00:16:54,067 --> 00:16:55,533
Don't kill me!

349
00:16:55,533 --> 00:16:56,833
[PANTING]

350
00:16:56,833 --> 00:16:58,700
Don't kill me!
I'll give you money!

351
00:17:02,333 --> 00:17:09,333
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

352
00:17:11,133 --> 00:17:13,433
Help! Help! Help me!

353
00:17:13,433 --> 00:17:14,933
Help me!

354
00:17:14,967 --> 00:17:17,467
Hey, you!
You're the father of Victor!

355
00:17:17,467 --> 00:17:19,000
You've come to rescue me?

356
00:17:19,000 --> 00:17:21,567
Rescue me. Help me.
Please. Please help me.

357
00:17:22,467 --> 00:17:24,000
I would like to.

358
00:17:24,000 --> 00:17:24,867
Please.

359
00:17:24,867 --> 00:17:26,800
- No! No! No!
- [GUN COCKS]

360
00:17:26,800 --> 00:17:28,367
- No!
- [GUN FIRES]

361
00:17:28,367 --> 00:17:29,333
[BODY THUDS]

362
00:17:31,600 --> 00:17:33,067
But I won't.

363
00:17:34,833 --> 00:17:35,900
Let's go.

364
00:17:35,900 --> 00:17:42,900
[DARK MUSIC PLAYING]

365
00:17:48,833 --> 00:17:50,667
[ENGINE REVS]

366
00:17:57,633 --> 00:17:59,033
Thank you for doing this.

367
00:17:59,833 --> 00:18:02,333
I'm doing this for the agency,
Pia.

368
00:18:02,333 --> 00:18:04,033
I know.

369
00:18:04,033 --> 00:18:07,033
I just want to thank you

370
00:18:07,033 --> 00:18:10,433
for considering my review
and recommendation

371
00:18:10,433 --> 00:18:12,933
regarding Jacinto's case.

372
00:18:12,933 --> 00:18:14,000
Well,

373
00:18:14,000 --> 00:18:16,833
we don't have sufficient grounds
for dismissal.

374
00:18:16,833 --> 00:18:20,567
Especially since Jacinto
arrested a vital witness.

375
00:18:20,567 --> 00:18:23,867
The important thing is that
the administrative case

376
00:18:23,900 --> 00:18:25,767
against Jacinto
is moving forward.

377
00:18:25,767 --> 00:18:27,367
Thanks to you.

378
00:18:27,367 --> 00:18:34,200
[FOREBODING MUSIC PLAYING]

379
00:18:36,700 --> 00:18:41,000
Gabo, we will give you
everything you need.

380
00:18:41,000 --> 00:18:46,100
Equipment, money,
weapons, and transportation.

381
00:18:46,100 --> 00:18:49,167
Everything you'll need
for your mission.

382
00:18:49,800 --> 00:18:52,900
You need to operate undetected.

383
00:18:54,633 --> 00:18:58,800
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

384
00:18:58,833 --> 00:19:01,833
Prepare everything
Gabo will need.

385
00:19:03,833 --> 00:19:04,833
Follow me.

386
00:19:04,833 --> 00:19:08,400
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

387
00:19:08,400 --> 00:19:09,467
[POCKET KNIFE CLINKS]

388
00:19:15,100 --> 00:19:16,033
[GLASSES CLINK]

389
00:19:16,033 --> 00:19:17,267
What?!

390
00:19:17,267 --> 00:19:23,667
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

391
00:19:23,667 --> 00:19:26,233
Yes, I will handle
things from my end.

392
00:19:26,233 --> 00:19:33,067
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

393
00:19:33,833 --> 00:19:34,800
David.

394
00:19:34,800 --> 00:19:35,900
Sir.

395
00:19:36,900 --> 00:19:39,567
Mr. Chan's convoy was ambushed.

396
00:19:39,567 --> 00:19:41,200
Shut down all routes.

397
00:19:41,200 --> 00:19:45,433
Gather all CCTV
and traffic camera footage.

398
00:19:45,433 --> 00:19:50,800
FInd out who
ambushed the convoy.

399
00:19:50,800 --> 00:19:53,300
If you need to go through
every second of footage, do it.

400
00:19:53,300 --> 00:19:58,000
And call the families
of our fallen colleagues.

401
00:19:58,000 --> 00:20:04,000
Let them know that
their loved one died a hero.

402
00:20:04,033 --> 00:20:08,033
And let them know
that we will help them.

403
00:20:08,033 --> 00:20:08,933
Now, move!

404
00:20:08,933 --> 00:20:10,300
- Yes, sir!
- Yes, sir!

405
00:20:11,533 --> 00:20:13,967
Sir, what happened?

406
00:20:13,967 --> 00:20:16,533
Team Bravo was ambushed.

407
00:20:16,533 --> 00:20:18,100
No one survived.

408
00:20:19,667 --> 00:20:21,467
Even Mr. Chan.

409
00:20:21,467 --> 00:20:28,533
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

410
00:20:28,533 --> 00:20:32,000
Team, we have a big problem.

411
00:20:32,000 --> 00:20:35,167
Team Bravo was ambushed
while escorting Mr. Chan.

412
00:20:35,200 --> 00:20:36,500
They were all killed.

413
00:20:36,500 --> 00:20:39,000
I am sure the Zafras
are behind this ambush.

414
00:20:39,000 --> 00:20:40,900
We are up against
a dangerous group.

415
00:20:40,900 --> 00:20:43,600
They attacked in broad daylight.

416
00:20:43,600 --> 00:20:45,133
If Mr. Chan is dead,

417
00:20:45,133 --> 00:20:47,100
Victor Safra won't be
implicated in the case

418
00:20:47,100 --> 00:20:48,767
because no one will
testify against him anymore.

419
00:20:48,767 --> 00:20:53,100
Mr. Chan was Sam's last hope,
and now he's dead.

420
00:20:53,100 --> 00:20:54,900
This is unacceptable.

421
00:20:54,900 --> 00:20:57,733
Mr. Chan was the only one
who could've saved Sam's job.

422
00:20:57,733 --> 00:21:02,567
But how did they find out
Mr. Chan was being transferred?

423
00:21:02,567 --> 00:21:07,800
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

424
00:21:07,800 --> 00:21:09,067
[SEBASTIAN] Sir!

425
00:21:10,333 --> 00:21:13,433
What happened?
How is this possible?

426
00:21:13,433 --> 00:21:16,867
Sir, if you let me handle
Mr. Chan's transport,

427
00:21:16,867 --> 00:21:18,033
this wouldn't happen!

428
00:21:18,033 --> 00:21:21,033
Are you telling me
what I should have done?!

429
00:21:21,033 --> 00:21:22,100
Yes, sir!

430
00:21:23,033 --> 00:21:26,733
I told you,
but you didn't listen!

431
00:21:26,733 --> 00:21:27,933
[SEBASTIAN EXHALES HEAVILY]

432
00:21:27,933 --> 00:21:29,167
Sir, I'm sorry.

433
00:21:29,167 --> 00:21:31,267
I'm trying to fix
Sam's problem,

434
00:21:31,267 --> 00:21:32,600
but you ruined everything!

435
00:21:32,600 --> 00:21:34,467
Watch your mouth!

436
00:21:34,467 --> 00:21:36,100
[RALLOS] Sir, sir, sir, sir.

437
00:21:36,100 --> 00:21:37,667
Uh-- Our apologies, sir.

438
00:21:37,667 --> 00:21:39,933
But Sir Sebastian's right.

439
00:21:39,933 --> 00:21:43,067
He should've handled
the transfer.

440
00:21:43,100 --> 00:21:48,033
Whoever took down
Mr. Chan and Team Bravo

441
00:21:48,033 --> 00:21:49,900
won't spare your life.

442
00:21:50,633 --> 00:21:54,267
You will suffer
the same fate as they did.

443
00:21:54,467 --> 00:21:58,333
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

444
00:21:58,333 --> 00:22:00,400
Hey. What's the matter?

445
00:22:01,633 --> 00:22:03,333
Bad news.

446
00:22:03,333 --> 00:22:05,100
Really bad news.

447
00:22:05,100 --> 00:22:06,633
Why? What happened?

448
00:22:06,633 --> 00:22:08,900
Mr. Chan's convoy was ambushed.

449
00:22:08,900 --> 00:22:11,000
They were transferring him
to a safe house.

450
00:22:11,000 --> 00:22:13,700
- But they never made it.
- [BREATHES HEAVILY]

451
00:22:13,700 --> 00:22:16,300
What happened to our
colleagues and Mr. Chan?

452
00:22:17,133 --> 00:22:19,333
They were all killed.

453
00:22:20,600 --> 00:22:21,867
Sorry, Sam.

454
00:22:21,867 --> 00:22:23,333
Mr. Chan is dead.

455
00:22:23,333 --> 00:22:27,833
[GRIM MUSIC PLAYING]

456
00:22:27,833 --> 00:22:29,267
The Zafras.

457
00:22:29,267 --> 00:22:31,400
The Zafras are behind this.

458
00:22:32,267 --> 00:22:34,867
That's it. We're screwed.

459
00:22:34,867 --> 00:22:39,033
The only person who can
help us solve this case is gone!

460
00:22:46,300 --> 00:22:48,233
- Sam.
- Sam!

461
00:22:49,033 --> 00:22:50,133
Sam!

462
00:22:50,133 --> 00:22:54,200
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

463
00:22:55,533 --> 00:22:57,167
- Where is Zafra?
- He's inside, Ma'am.

464
00:22:59,667 --> 00:23:00,833
Zafra!

465
00:23:00,833 --> 00:23:02,133
You son of a bitch.

466
00:23:02,133 --> 00:23:03,633
You're behind all of this.

467
00:23:03,633 --> 00:23:05,000
What did I do?

468
00:23:05,000 --> 00:23:06,300
What are you talking about?

469
00:23:06,300 --> 00:23:07,800
Mr. Chan is dead.

470
00:23:07,800 --> 00:23:08,933
[CHUCKLES]

471
00:23:11,233 --> 00:23:13,533
I'm locked up in here,
and you're going to accuse me?

472
00:23:14,567 --> 00:23:16,233
Didn't you try to kill him?

473
00:23:16,233 --> 00:23:18,467
Now they're transferring him
so he could testify.

474
00:23:18,467 --> 00:23:20,033
But he got ambushed.

475
00:23:20,033 --> 00:23:22,333
I know someone on the outside
is working for you.

476
00:23:22,367 --> 00:23:24,933
The moment I find out
your parents were involved,

477
00:23:24,933 --> 00:23:26,900
all of you are going to rot
in prison.

478
00:23:26,900 --> 00:23:28,733
And even if I lose my position,

479
00:23:28,733 --> 00:23:31,433
I'll do everything
to bring the truth to light.

480
00:23:33,933 --> 00:23:35,967
Why don't you arrest
the long-haired guy?

481
00:23:37,267 --> 00:23:40,000
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

482
00:23:40,733 --> 00:23:42,267
Mr. Chan said

483
00:23:43,400 --> 00:23:45,000
he was the one
who caught him, too.

484
00:23:45,000 --> 00:23:46,500
The guy I fought in Chinatown?

485
00:23:46,500 --> 00:23:47,733
You know that guy?

486
00:23:47,733 --> 00:23:50,100
That's for me to know,
and for you to find out.

487
00:23:50,100 --> 00:23:51,633
It's a race between us now,
Jacinto,

488
00:23:51,633 --> 00:23:53,900
because once I get
out of here, I'll come for you.

489
00:23:53,900 --> 00:23:56,300
Not just you, but the man
who put me in prison, too.

490
00:23:57,467 --> 00:23:58,767
Now do your job.

491
00:24:02,700 --> 00:24:09,533
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

492
00:24:24,433 --> 00:24:31,267
[MUSIC BECOMES PENSIVE]

493
00:24:38,767 --> 00:24:41,033
<i>- You're crazy!
- You're beautiful.</i>

494
00:24:41,500 --> 00:24:42,567
<i> What's your name?</i>

495
00:24:42,567 --> 00:24:44,333
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

496
00:24:45,167 --> 00:24:46,400
<i> Excuse me.</i>

497
00:24:46,400 --> 00:24:47,667
<i>- Ouch!
- You again?</i>

498
00:24:48,667 --> 00:24:50,433
[VICTOR] Why don't you arrest
the long-haired guy?

499
00:24:50,433 --> 00:24:52,167
<i>- Stop!
- [GUNSHOT]</i>

500
00:24:52,167 --> 00:24:54,133
<i> The guy I fought in Chinatown?</i>

501
00:24:54,133 --> 00:24:55,267
[GUNSHOTS]

502
00:24:55,967 --> 00:24:58,867
<i>Mr. Chan said he was
the one who caught him, too.</i>

503
00:25:00,033 --> 00:25:01,867
[SAM] The long-haired guy?

504
00:25:03,333 --> 00:25:06,067
<i>Could he also be the man
who stole a kiss from me?</i>

505
00:25:06,933 --> 00:25:09,767
<i>And the man I saw
at the Chinese lawyer's bar?</i>

506
00:25:12,133 --> 00:25:14,500
<i>He seems to know a lot
about this case.</i>

507
00:25:16,200 --> 00:25:18,233
<i> Is he an ally or an enemy?</i>

508
00:25:20,067 --> 00:25:21,833
<i> I need to find him.</i>

509
00:25:21,833 --> 00:25:28,667
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

510
00:25:53,600 --> 00:25:54,600
<i> What, Samantha?!</i>

511
00:25:54,600 --> 00:25:55,967
<i> Are you still alive?!</i>

512
00:25:57,367 --> 00:25:59,000
<i> That's what you'll use</i>

513
00:25:59,000 --> 00:26:01,967
<i>against anyone who goes up
against you face-to-face.</i>

514
00:26:02,533 --> 00:26:06,500
<i> I will let you handle BeerGin.</i>

515
00:26:06,500 --> 00:26:09,567
<i>If you really get to Betchay,
she might finally talk.</i>

516
00:26:10,033 --> 00:26:12,133
<i>She'll tell us what Gabo's
real job is.</i>

517
00:26:12,133 --> 00:26:14,900
<i>It's not just Victor's freedom
that's at stake here,</i>

518
00:26:14,900 --> 00:26:17,067
<i> but the entire organization.</i>

519
00:26:17,067 --> 00:26:18,267
<i> When I come back here,</i>

520
00:26:18,267 --> 00:26:20,867
<i>I'll be carrying
that Samantha Jacinto's head.</i>

521
00:26:20,867 --> 00:26:22,967
<i>Admit that you're involved
in this.</i>

522
00:26:22,967 --> 00:26:25,000
<i>Admit that your family
is involved.</i>

523
00:26:25,000 --> 00:26:28,133
<i> You never should've
brought her into your world!</i>

524
00:26:28,133 --> 00:26:30,767
<i> Ricardo, I lost one child!</i>

525
00:26:30,767 --> 00:26:34,433
<i>And I can't bear
to lose another!</i>

526
00:26:34,433 --> 00:26:35,833
<i> Don't let her escape!</i>

527
00:26:35,833 --> 00:26:38,233
<i>I need intel on where
we can find the Zafras.</i>

528
00:26:38,233 --> 00:26:39,300
<i> They will pay.</i>

529
00:26:39,300 --> 00:26:42,167
<i>We're talking about
the life of my agent!</i>

530
00:26:42,200 --> 00:26:45,633
<i>If you're losing agents,
don't look for someone to blame!</i>

531
00:26:45,633 --> 00:26:47,433
Can you do it? Pull the trigger!

532
00:26:49,467 --> 00:26:52,600
She's our snake inside the NCIA.

533
00:26:52,600 --> 00:26:56,200
<i>A snake?
I'm your ace.</i>

534
00:26:56,200 --> 00:26:57,800
<i>Something suddenly fell
onto our roof.</i>

535
00:26:57,800 --> 00:26:59,267
<i>What was that?
Where did it come from?</i>

536
00:26:59,267 --> 00:27:00,500
<i> That person suddenly fell.</i>

537
00:27:00,500 --> 00:27:01,600
<i> She's in danger.</i>

538
00:27:01,600 --> 00:27:03,567
We need to help and protect her.

539
00:27:03,567 --> 00:27:10,467
["TUNAY NA LIGAYA"
BY JUAN KARLOS PLAYING]

540
00:27:18,600 --> 00:27:20,833
Coco Martin's Sigabo!
